abstract: >-
  DEMM-Bench is a cross-regime governance-evidence sufficiency benchmark for
  agent-runtime decisions. It normalises eight evidence regimes (AER, MAT,
  IEEC, DCC/HDP, PROV, LLM Audit Trails, AEGIS-NTC, Dynamic Capabilities)
  through adapters, applies eight deterministic degradation conditions, and
  scores governance-question reconstructability with five default
  container-presence baselines and one redacted property-level candidate
  scorer. Primary metrics are Property Sufficiency Accuracy and Overclaim
  Rate. The deposited 64-case manuscript package reports trace-present and
  schema-present baselines overclaiming on 75% of cases, ledger-present on
  50%, and the candidate scorer achieving 56.25% mean PSA with zero
  overclaim and paired-oracle Cohen kappa of 1.0.
